Root cause: The header component incorrectly hides the navigation menu from assistive technology when the menu button is collapsed (aria-expanded false) regardless of viewport, causing navigation links to be omitted from the accessibility tree on desktop where the menu is visually visible.

Repair strategy: Modify syncState to conditionally apply aria-hidden only when the menu button is visible (mobile) and the menu is not open; otherwise ensure menu is exposed.

Expected accessibility effect: Navigation links will be exposed as links with correct accessible names, allowing screen readers and keyboard users to reach them.

Functional risks: Potential double hiding/showing if CSS changes; reliance on computed style may fail if menuButton display changes dynamically; but low risk.

Verification requirements: Test that on desktop width, navigation links have role link and name; on mobile width, menu button toggles visibility and aria-hidden behaves correctly; ensure menu button aria-expanded toggles; ensure no regression in menu open/close behavior.

